# Lab 11: MLOps Pipeline

## 1. Pipeline Workflow

Data → Preprocessing → Training → Evaluation → Deployment → Monitoring

## 2. Tools Used

- Python
- MLflow
- Scikit-learn

## 3. Experiment Logging

MLflow was used to log:
- Parameters (model type, max_iter)
- Metrics (accuracy)
- Model artifacts

## 4. Model Versioning

Two versions were created:
- Version 1: max_iter = 200
- Version 2: max_iter = 100

Each run in MLflow represents a new version.

## 5. Best Model

The model with higher accuracy was selected as the best model.

## 6. Rollback Strategy

If the new model performs worse:
- Previous stable model is used
- System switches back to older version
- Performance is monitored

## 7. Conclusion

This lab demonstrated how MLflow helps in:
- Tracking experiments
- Managing model versions
- Ensuring safe deployment using rollback